Q: Dynamically fit two divs with different overflow types A: <p>Okay here is what I did</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>body {
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100vh;
  width: 100vw;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  overflow-x: hidden;

  background-color: #ccf;
}

#left-container {
  width: 40%;
  background-color: #030;
  color: #fff;
}

#right-container {
  width: 60%;
  height: 100vh;
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  overflow: auto;

  background-color: #300;
  color: #fff;
}

#left-container div {
  height: 2000px;
  width: 80%;
  margin: auto;
  background-image: linear-gradient(#082, #06a);
}

#right-container div {
  height: 3000px;
  width: 80%;
  margin: auto;
  background-image: linear-gradient(#820, #990);
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="left-container"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div id="right-container"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>In <code>body</code> I changed from <code>height: 100vh</code> to <code>min-height: 100vh</code> - this allows the body to grow beyond viewport height. Removed the <code>min-height: fit-content</code>. This is not needed since body will naturally fit its content.</p>
<p>In <code>left-container</code> removed <code>min-height: fit-content</code> and <code>height: 100%</code> because the container will now naturally expand with it's content</p>
<p>in <code>right-container</code> added <code>position: sticky</code> with <code>top: 0</code> to keep it fixed at viewport height while the page scrolls. Also changed the <code>height: 100%</code> to <code>height: 100vh</code> to get a definite viewport height. Kept <code>overflow: auto</code> to allow internal scrolling for the <code>3000px</code> content</p>
<p>Hope this what you were looking for</p>

Q: Table &#39;tblCustomer&#39; does not have the identity property. Cannot perform SET operation A: <p>Just comment out <code>DatabaseGenerated</code> line, it is not required.</p>
<p>And check your database, it seems Migrations or some SQL against database has enabled identity column inside your database when you first created it, you need to remove Identity.</p>
<p>It may be a bug in migrations. Delete the database and try again.</p>
<pre><code>public class Customer
{
    [Key]
    [Required]
    // comment following, you don't need to specify anything
    // [DatabaseGenerated(DatabaseGeneratedOption.none)]
    public string CustomerCode { get; set; }

    [Required]
    [StringLength(10)]
    [RegularExpression(&quot;^[A-Z]{7,7}$&quot;)]
    public string CustomerName { get; set; }
}
</code></pre>
